{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens' tree coverage is one of the city's defining features — the towering oaks lining streets near the courthouse square, the mature maples shading neighborhoods around Athens State University, the pecan trees in backyards throughout the county. That canopy provides shade, character, and natural beauty that newer subdivisions can't replicate.</p>

<p>But every one of those trees drops debris directly into your gutters. In fall, it's a deluge of leaves — large oak leaves, smaller maple leaves, pecan shells and stems. In spring, it's seeds, pollen, and helicopter pods. Year-round, it's twigs from wind and storms. Athens homeowners often find themselves cleaning gutters 3-4 times per year just to keep up.</p>

<p>Many try DIY cleaning, which means weekends spent on ladders. Others pay $150-200 per professional cleaning — that's $600-800 annually for a chore that never ends. Meanwhile, between cleanings, clogged gutters overflow during heavy rains, sending water cascading down siding and pooling around foundations.</p>

<p>Gutter guards change the equation entirely. Instead of an ongoing battle against debris, you install guards once and the problem is solved. Water enters your gutters; leaves, twigs, and debris slide off or sit harmlessly on top. Your gutters do their job year after year with virtually no maintenance.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to flow through while blocking leaves, seeds, twigs, and other debris. The technology varies by type, but the goal is the same: keep gutters clear without constant cleaning.</p>

<p>Different guard types work better for different debris. Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pecan shells and seed pods. Screen guards handle larger oak and maple leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off the edge.</p>

<p>For most Athens homes — especially those in established neighborhoods with mixed tree coverage — we recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris effectively, and they're tough enough to withstand the weight of heavy leaf accumulation. During your free estimate, we'll assess your specific tree situation and recommend the right solution for your home.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been installing gutter guards in Athens and throughout Limestone County for over 20 years. We know which systems work best for the area's specific mix of oak, maple, and pecan debris — and which products are just marketing hype.</p>

<p>We're not a national franchise pushing a one-size-fits-all solution. We're North Alabama locals who understand that the tree coverage near Athens State University is different from the newer subdivisions, and that historic downtown homes have different needs than modern construction. That local knowledge means you get the right guards for your specific situation, not whatever product has the biggest advertising budget.</p>
